<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Derivative of a quadratic from first principles (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In this question you differentiate \( f(x) = {@fexpr@} \) <b>from first principles</b>, one step at a time. Give exact answers (no decimals).</p>
<p><b>Step 1.</b> Expand \( f(x+h) \) fully:</p>
<div>\( f(x+h) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><b>Step 2.</b> Form the difference quotient and simplify it by cancelling the factor \( h \):</p>
<div>\( \displaystyle\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><b>Step 3.</b> Let \( h \to 0 \) to obtain the derivative:</p>
<div>\( \displaystyle f'(x) = \lim_{h \to 0}\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p><b>Step 4.</b> Hence find the value of the derivative at \( x = {@x0@} \):</p>
<div>\( f'({@x0@}) = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Step 1.</b> Expand \( f(x+h) \), being careful with the cross term in \( (x+h)^2 \):</p>
\[
f(x+h) = {@fxh_unexp@} = {@fxh_true@}.
\]
<p><b>Step 2.</b> Subtract \( f(x) \) and cancel the common factor \( h \). Every term of the numerator carries an \( h \), so the cancellation is valid because we do it <em>before</em> letting \( h \to 0 \):</p>
\[
\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h} = \frac{{@num_collected@}}{h} = {@quot_true@}.
\]
<p><b>Step 3.</b> As \( h \to 0 \) the term \( {@drop_term@} \) vanishes, leaving the derivative:</p>
\[
f'(x) = \lim_{h \to 0}\left({@quot_true@}\right) = {@lim_true@}.
\]
<p><b>Step 4.</b> Substitute \( x = {@x0@} \):</p>
\[
f'({@x0@}) = {@lim_sub@} = {@fp_x0_true@}.
\]
<p>The middle term \( 2ax\,h \) comes from the cross term in \( (x+h)^2 = x^2 + 2xh + h^2 \); dropping it is the most common slip. Notice too that the constant coefficient of \( x^2 \) becomes a factor of \( 2 \) in the derivative - this is the pattern the power rule will make into a shortcut.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
